e defect GEOS reports.\n2. **A degenerate spike along the diagonal** — the excursion `(0,0) → (1,1) → (0,0)` doubles back on itself across the square's interior, so the boundary is not a simple closed curve and the polygon's interior is not well-defined.\n\nThe violation is confined to the single **exterior** ring of the single feature (`features[0]`, `\"name\": \"test\"`), with the reported intersection point at coordinate **(0, 0)**.\n\n### How to fix it\n\nA valid version simply drops the spike and closes the ring once:\n\n```json\n\"coordinates\": [[[0,0],[2,0],[2,2],[0,2],[0,0]]]\n```\n\nIf you'd like, I can write the corrected file or add a small validation script as a test fixture."